healing with the touch of a horse local  non-profit horses for heroes has made  that its mission and this weekend  they're hoping to spread awareness on  this very special type of therapy  victoria saha has the story  horses for heroes a non-profit ranch  helping our veterans cope with the  aftermath of combat i knew there was  something missing  but it wasn't anything that i could  describe jessica white is a navy veteran  and also a volunteer at the ranch it  took her 10 years to get back on a horse  after returning home it was freeing and  it made me just so happy that feeling of  euphoria is something white wants all  veterans to experience at a time where  they may feel nothing at all they  comfort you  and they will  bring you in like one of their own which  is why she's taking part in a three-day  certification course in equine assisted  learning held by greg kirsten they start  seeing  that they can do different things in  order to keep themselves safe kirsten a  veteran himself studies wild horses in  nevada he watched how they fend for  themselves and go through distress when  separated from their herd similar to  veterans transitioning from warrior life  to civilian life we still are working  with vietnam era veterans all the horses  here come from different backgrounds  just like our servicemen and women and  having that connection is so special for  equine therapy creating a strong bond  only the both of you can understand  everything you're thinking the horse  feels everything the horse  thinks you're feeling because it's just  you and that horse victoria saha live  local now
 

